        "What experiments do you suggest doing?": [
            "1. Needle in a haystack test: The authors should use their proposed SLED model and other related baselines on the needle in a haystack tests. They can form such a test by transforming an existing question answering (QA) dataset such as SQuAD to a long input QA task. For example, for each original question-paragraph pair, the authors can randomly sample some other paragraphs from the dataset as distractor texts and concatenate them to form a long document. Then evaluate models\u2019 performance on this long input QA task. They should also conduct the experiments with different distractors orders.",
            "2. Evaluation of the SLED ability to fuse information from different chunks: The authors should evaluate SLED and other related baselines about the ability of fusing information from the inputs. They should design a task that the models need to solve by fusing the information from at least two different text segments. For example, they can use HotpotQA, in which every question relies on two pieces of information (located in different paragraphs).",
            "3. The necessity of local textualization in encoder: The authors should check whether it is possible for all fusion to occur in the decoder. For example, they can finetune SLED with a chunk size of c = 1, such that input tokens do not observe any context in the encoder.",
            "4. The effect of contextualizing chunks with a prefix: The authors should finetune a SLED model that treats the prefix as another chunk and does not prepend it to document chunks.",
            "5. The effect of prefix tokens on the decoder: The authors should finetune SLED as usual but remove the prefix tokens from the final representation given to the decoder.",
            "6. Long text understanding performance comparison: The authors should compare the performance of SLED with other long text understanding models. It is also necessary to compare SLED with the short text backbone models used. The authors should conduct the experiments on various long text understanding tasks such as summarization and question answering. Moreover, they also need to apply SLED to different encoder-decoder models and show the performance.",
            "7. Analyze the effect locality of information on different datasets using SLED: The authors can use SLED to analyze locality. They can vary the chunk size of SLED while fixing the maximum input length and measure the effect on different types of datasets such as summarization and question answering.",
            "8. The influence of SLED input length on different datasets: The authors should vary the input length fed to SLED and report its performance on different datasets.",
            "9. Effect of context padding: The authors should finetune SLED on the datasets where SLED showed gains over its baseline model, varying the number of context padding tokens, and fixing the chunk size."
        ],
        "Why do you suggest these experiments?": [
            "1. To check if SLED can locate a piece of short information embedded in long text, disregarding irrelevant information.",
            "2. To verify that SLED can fuse pieces of information from different chunks.",
